(For PDM_CLK and PDM data signals:) Tj
T* (   - Avoid long single-line daisy chains where the last microphone is at the end of a long stub.) Tj
T* (   - Use a balanced tree / star topology branching out from the TSDP1808 to the mics ) Tj
T* (        to keep trace distances reasonably balanced naturally.) Tj
T* (  - Match the PDM_CLK and pdm mic data trace lengths within 5mm of each other across ) Tj
T* (       all mics on this page.) Tj
T* (  - Maintain a minimum of 3x trace-width spacing between PDM Clock and Data traces, ) Tj
T* (     or run a continuous ground plane directly beneath all PDM routing layers.) Tj
T* (  - Avoid routing high-speed PDM clock lines over gaps or splits in the underlying ground plane.) Tj
