(Confirm in layout that PAD has multiple vias down to ground plane.) Tj
T* (PGND and GND. Both grounds must be connected on the PCB at only one point, ideally close to the GND pin.) Tj
T* (Keep the high-current path \(Battery \(-\) to Input/Output Caps to PGND pin & thermal pad\) contained on a tight copper pour. ) Tj
T* (Connect Pin 9 \(GND\) to this main ground pour at only a single point right next to the IC.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (transition from Schematic to PCB:) Tj
T* (PGND and GND are connected at a single star-point right at the thermal pad \(Pin 11\) / Pin 9 on the PCB.) Tj
T* (Treat them as the same net in the PCB layout editor \(or connect PGND and GND pads directly at the IC\).) Tj
T* (Pour a single, continuous Ground Plane on the bottom layer of PCB.) Tj
T* (Keep the  physical loops tight:) Tj
T* (Place C53 right next to Pin 5 \(VIN\) and Pin 3 \(PGND\).  ) Tj
T* (Place C52 and C51 right next to Pin 1 \(VOUT\) and Pin 3 \(PGND\).  ) Tj
T* (Place C54 right next to Pin 8 \(VINA\) and Pin 9 \(GND\).) Tj
T* (Keep trace loops from Pin 5 \(VIN\) to C53 to Pin 3 \(PGND\), and Pin 1 \(VOUT\) to C52/C51 to Pin 3 \(PGND\) as ) Tj
T* (short and wide as possible to prevent EMI and stability issues.) Tj
